\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown up, seen testing stronger levels. \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2002\par 09:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  was slightly stronger against the euro in moderate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Tuesday morning activity, and dealers said the unit had \par \par \uc2  potential for further gains in the near future. \par \par \uc2      The crown was quoted at 42.16/20 to the euro as of 0830 GMT, \par \par \uc2  after 42.20/24 at Monday's close. It was at 48.60/65 to the \par \par \uc2  dollar, from 48.45/51. \par \par \uc2      The market is eagerly awaiting Wednesday's government \par \par \uc2  session, in which the Cabinet is widely expected to reject a \par \par \uc2  controversial proposal to signifcantly alter crucial sale of \par \par \uc2  natural gas company SPP. \par \par \uc2      "We expect the government will announce the (SPP) sale will \par \par \uc2  proceed in line with original plans and this will be a strong \par \par \uc2  impetus for the crown to firm sharply," Volksbank said in a \par \par \uc2  research note on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      On Monday, Premier Mikulas Dzurinda said the sale would go \par \par \uc2  on as planned, but the leftist coalition SDL party promised to \par \par \uc2  present its proposal, which leaders of the ruling coalition have \par \par \uc2  already rejected, at Wednesday's government meeting. \par \par \uc2      While the government aims to find a new owner for 49 percent \par \par \uc2  and management rights in SPP in a tender due to close at the end \par \par \uc2  of this month, SDL wants to change the sale so that only 24 \par \par \uc2  percent of SPP is sold. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise could be held in \par \par \uc2  check by movements of the Czech crown, which has been edgy in \par \par \uc2  the past few days amid threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown is expected to move between 42.00-42.30 per \par \par \uc2  euro in coming days, with traders saying the unit was likely to \par \par \uc2  test the 42.10 level on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020219dy2j00hlo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
