\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Euro moves main driver for Europe,rand. \b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2001\par 12:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe recovered some ground against the euro on Friday but remained under its spell as the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose across the board amid expectations that euro-zone growth will outpace the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The euro's push to a fresh six-month high against the dollar provided the backbone for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise to a 2-1/2 month peak against the Czech crown, a one-month top against the zloty and a lifetime high against the South African rand. \par \par \uc2  However, emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held firm against the dollar which has seen its support fade as concerns over the U.S. economy's health overshadowed the stock market-led rally that followed Wednesday's surprise U.S. interest rate cut. \par \par \uc2  "It's still the euro and dollar that's guiding emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment. It's a good environment for traders but it's still too frothy to pull in more long-term investors," said one U.S. bank emerging market analyst. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty was trading at 4.0850 per dollar to the dollar from 4.1151 late on Thursday. Against the euro, the zloty stood at 3.8976 after earlier touching a one-month low of 3.9259. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown slipped to 35.34 per euro, its weakest point against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since October 19. Against the dollar, the crown stood at 36.94 after earlier touching a new nine-month peak around 36.67. \par \par \uc2  Both Czech and Polish bond prices extended their gains amid ongoing expectations of slowing inflation and forthcoming interest rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak crown edged lower against the euro but dealers said the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown on one side and a market short of euros on the other would likely keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a tight range. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday and Wednesday to keep the crown from slipping past the 44 per euro level, saying its weakness did not reflect Slovakia's macroeconomic position. \par \par \uc2  The crown stood at 43.85/90 to the euro from 43.77/85 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The rand was last bid at 7.48 per dollar, still shy of this week's two month highs but bolstered by gains made by the euro - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of South Africa's major trading partners - against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the rand's drop to a new record low against the buoyant euro would keep dollar/rand gains in check until there was more foreign investment in South African assets. \par \par \uc2  So far, foreigners have been wary of jumping into South Africa despite South African bond yields hitting their lowest level in seven years amid expectations that domestic interest rates could be cut early this year. \par \par \uc2  Local banks and institutions piled into government debt, sending yields - which move in the opposite direction to prices - on the benchmark R150 bond, due February 2005, to 11.82 percent, its lowest point since January 1994. \par \par \uc2  A combination of lower bond yields, a firm rand and easing oil prices have boosted chances that the Reserve Bank could cut rates when its interest-rate setting Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) starts a two-day meeting on January 18, traders said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1505sw3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
