\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -E.Europe extends rally on soft dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2001\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 2 (Reuters) - Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe started the new year strongly against the dollar on Tuesday as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a five-month low against a broadly stronger euro. \par \par \uc2  The zloty extended December's rally and hit an 8-1/2 month high against the dollar while the Czech crown rallied to an eight month peak and the South African rand also posted gains. \par \par \uc2  However, the buoyant euro, boosted by expectations the euro zone economy will be relative strong while there is a sharp slowdown in the United States and Japan, rose against the rand and emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe. \par \par \uc2  The stronger euro prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the crown , buying crowns from the 44 per euro level. The crown was trading at 43.87/95 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was satisfied with the outcome of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but did not reveal the volume of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered by the bank. \par \par \uc2  Recent European data have reinforced the view that euro-zone growth remains relatively robust and it is well placed to withstand a period of slower global growth. This has provided a key support for emerging Europe which sends most of its exports to the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  The zloty stood at 4.1000 per dollar from 4.145 late on Friday and at 3.8753 to the euro against 3.852. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was awaiting the release of Polish current account data at 1500 GMT. A Reuters consensus poll conducted at the start of December showed analysts expecting the current account gap to fall some some $800 million in November from $1.05 billion in October. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown rose to its highest level against the dollar since March 28 last year but edged lower against the euro, trading at 35.11 to the euro after briefly firming to 34.95. \par \par \uc2  The crown stood at 37.14/17 per dollar from 37.60/63 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  South Africa's rand edged up against the weaker dollar, last bid at 7.5675 per dollar from 7.5680 in late South African trade before New Year break. \par \par \uc2  The rand struggled against the stronger euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of South Africa's major trading partners, and was last quoted at around 7.1560 per euro from 7.03. Against sterling the rand was trading at at 11.28. \par \par \uc2  The yield on South Africa's benchmark R150 bond was last bid at 12.075 percent from its 12.01 percent close last Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1206t32\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
