\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank ready to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to support crown. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Javurek \par \uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2000\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Oct 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBS) Governor Marian Jusko said on Tuesday that the bank was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown if it continued to weaken against the euro. \par \par \uc2  "The crown has depreciated against the euro by 3.3 percent since the beginning of the year... In case of continued weakening of the crown, we are ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Jusko told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  NBS Vice Governor Elena Kohutikova said the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with 45 million euros on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last month to support the crown. \par \par \uc2  "It was a so-called 'discreet' type of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she added without elaborating. \par \par \uc2  The crown has declined to lows not seen in nearly a year, following the announcement of a November 11 referendum on whether to hold early general elections. \par \par \uc2  It traded at 43.94/02 to the euro on Tuesday morning, from 43.88/94 late on Monday and bid at around 42.60 in mid-September. \par \par \uc2  "We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the crown exchange rate development does not reflect the macroeconomic indicators... which are favourable at the moment," Jusko said. \par \par \uc2  Jusko also said that the bank would consider cutting interest rates further, following a reduction at the end of August, only after next year's budget had been set. The NBS board decided on September 29 to leave interest rates unchanged. On August 30, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key overnight rate for sterilising \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 6.5 percent from 7.0 percent and its refinancing repo rate to 9.5 percent from 10.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The last time the bank board decided to keep interest rates unchanged, one of the reasons was uncertainty over next year's public finance," NBS Governor Marian Jusko told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "When the budget is set, and if the stable macroeconomic developments continue, then we may decide to lower interest rates... but it certainly won't be as much as last time," he added. \par \par \uc2  The government has agreed to set the 2001 state budget so that the overall public finance deficit does not exceed 4.0 percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  The cabinet plans to vote on the budget draft on October 4 and to submit it to the parliament for the final discussion by October 15. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa305scj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
