\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW-Slovak c.bank says fighting volatility. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2000\par 14:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, April 19 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's discreet \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  against crown strength are aimed at curbing volatility rather than defending a specific exchange rate, Vice-governor Elena Kohutikova said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  She added, in an interview with Reuters, that interest rates would not become a significant instrument in the management of the exchange rate. The overnight repo rate stands at 7.5 percent for sterilisation \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and 10.5 percent for refinancing. \par \par \uc2  "We see that the interest rates are at an acceptable level at present...We cannot subordinate interest rate policy to exchange rate policy," she said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used the equivalent of over $400 million this year to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly from local banks. The bank has voiced concerns that trade performance could be hurt if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed too much. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are designed to prevent certain volumes of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  from moving the exchange rate significantly for a few days," Kohutikova told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \uc2  When asked whether the bank was defending any particular crowns levels, she said: "No, we are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent volatility in the market." \par \par \uc2  She added there was no need at present for different forms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : "Of course, it's a matter for the bank board to decide, but for now we do not see a reason to use a different procedure." \par \par \uc2  Interest in the Slovak crown soared in December after the European Union formally invited the country to open accession talks. The pressure has been kept up due to expectations of large privatisations planned by the government for this year and next. \par \par \uc2  "Too much crown strengthening having to do with the capital account...would not be very good for the economy, so we have prepared some instruments to eliminate this effect," she said, referring to plans to set up special privatisation accounts from which \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows would be dissolved in the economy gradually. \par \par \uc2  "Negotiations are going on right now and there seems to be general support for the idea...The funds would be spread out to minimise the pressure on the crown," she said. \par \par \uc2  Kohutikova said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also remained prepared to sterilise the crown market as needed, regardless of costs. "We are sterilising huge amounts of money and are ready to sterilise enough to maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability." ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4j021u1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
