\par\par \b \uc2  WRAPUP 1-Slovak  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  battles on with strong crown. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrej Salner \par \uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2000\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, April 11 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to combat crown strength with market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is ready to keep expected privatisation inflows from boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Vice-Governor Elena Kohutikova said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Between December and mid-February the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying euros to prevent the crown from firming. \par \par \uc2  The recently appointed vice-governor told a management conference the bank was still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , albeit less overtly. \par \par \uc2  "We are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  discreetly in the market... continuously," she said, adding that the bank had so far bought the equivalent of $400 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2000. \par \par \uc2  These covert \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved directly buying large volumes of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from local banks. \par \par \uc2  The crown came under appreciation pressure in December when Slovakia received a formal invitation to open European Union accession talks. \par \par \uc2  Officials say they do not want it to strengthen in a way that could hit Slovakia's export-led growth and falling current account deficit, although they have allowed it to firm a little after stronger trade data. \par \par \uc2  Kohutikova said the bank was facing mounting pressure in its efforts to sterilise crown liquidity arising from the conversion of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows. \par \par \uc2  "I expect the sterilisation position (the amount currently borrowed by the bank from the crown market) could reach as much as 60 billion crowns ($1.4 billion) this year." Kohutikova said the figure currently stood at around 25 billion crowns. \par \par \uc2  Appreciation pressure on the crown has increased ahead of an extensive programme of sales of government holdings in banks and enterprises, expected to bring in tens of billions of crowns from foreign investors in the next two years. \par \par \uc2  "Towards the end of the year I expect the actual bank privatisation to begin, not only in state-owned banks but in smaller banks where the state has a share," Kohutikova said, adding that she expected the main privatisation wave next year. \par \par \uc2  "We are negotiating with the FNM (state privatisation agency) and the finance ministry on opening special accounts for these capital inflows...to stabilise these funds at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gradually dissolve them into the economy." \par \par \uc2  Kohutikova said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believed the 2000 current account deficit might come in lower than the 5.3 percent of GDP targeted. She forecast the deficit at 4.1 percent of GDP in 2001, 3.7 percent in 2002, 3.2 percent in 2003 and 2.8 percent in 2004. $=43.1 Slovak crowns ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4b02mem\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
