\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says not  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  to weaken crown. \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2000\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The head of the Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets department said on Monday that the bank had seen the crown firm through 42.000 to the euro and that it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't know of anyone from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  who said 42.000 was some level at which we would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Frantisek Szulenyi told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Several trades took place at 41.98 to the euro prior to Szulenyi's remarks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several occassions since mid December to stop the crown breaking through 42.3 to the euro but allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to firm through that level last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had speculated that the bank would probably step in if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened through 42.000. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say pressure for a firming has come mainly from the country's improved foreign trade performance. Positive sentiment had also been boosted by the prospect of Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development membership which ministers expect by the middle of the year at the latest. ((Robin Shepherd, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2s0693k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{