\par\par \b \uc2  Market mixed on Slovak rate move at cbank meeting. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robin Shepherd \par \uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2000\par 15:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Slovak dealers gave mixed views on Thursday at the liklehood of a repo rate change after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board meeting. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a new automatic repo system at the beginning of February setting the overnight rate for refinanicng at 12 percent and the sterilisation repo rate at 8.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dalibor Cernicka, managing director of Money Market Brokers in Bratislava, said a change in rates was unlikely precisely because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had only just introduced the new system. \par \par \uc2  "They could indicate the direction of rates but I think they would wait at least two months (for a change)," he said. \par \par \uc2  Miroslav Nespala from CSOB bank agreed. \par \par \uc2  "I would appreciate it if they narowed the spread to 8.5/11.5 but I don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do it tomorrow as it's only less than a month since they started this system," he said. \par \par \uc2  But others gave a different view. Rastislav Zivor, of ING Barings, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cut the sterilisation rate by 50-100 basis points. \par \par \uc2  "This would support the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been doing on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  until now. And it would make it cheaper to sterilise the market (after spending money on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed slightly earlier this week, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke with recent policy and allowed the crown to strengthen through the 42.3 to the euro level. It had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on several occassions to stop the crown firming over 42.3 since mid-December. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was traded between 42.14 and 42.2 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  ING's chief economist in Slovakia, Jan Toth, said a 50-100 basis point cut from 8.0 percent may come because the country's improved export performance lessened the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's need to keep the crown weak. \par \par \uc2  Foreign trade figures for January will be released on Friday morning. The finance and economy ministries have both said the figure will be slightly better than the 2.9 billion deficit recorded in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  The SITA news agency quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy head Elena Kohutikova on Thursday as saying Slovakia's current account deficit should fall to 5.6 percent of gross domestic product for 1999, 5.3 percent for 2000 and 4.1 percent of GDP in 2001. \par \par \uc2  ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2o06dpf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
