\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown steady in quiet trade, outlook stable. \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2000\par 10:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 23 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traded quietly on Wednesday morning, with dealers expecting no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  surprises throughout the day. \par \par \uc2      The crown was quoted at 42.150/190 to the euro at 0920 GMT, \par \par \uc2  unchanged from opening levels. \par \par \uc2      "Only the prices (of crown/\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) have been moving since the \par \par \uc2  open, but there were no real deals matched," said Roman Farkas \par \par \uc2  of Tatra Banka. \par \par \uc2      On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned its policy of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the crown from firming over 42.300 to the \par \par \uc2  euro. The bank has said it might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, but probably \par \par \uc2  at different levels of the crown/euro rate. \par \par \uc2  "The crown has a potential for further slight firming, \par \par \uc2  towards the 42.000 (to the euro) level, but I don't think this \par \par \uc2  will happen today," Farkas said. \par \par \uc2  "If there were any players willing to speculate, they would \par \par \uc2  have done it earlier, just after the market open," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Since nothing like that had happened, I don't expect any big \par \par \uc2  jumps later on today." \par \par \uc2  The crown was quoted at 41.980/022 to the dollar at 0925 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Javurek, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax \par \par \uc2  421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Do