\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown calm around cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  level. \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2000\par 10:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was quiet on Thursday morning, around levels where the central\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  bank has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a strengthening crown, dealers \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      The crown was quoted at 42.290/310 to the euro at 0900 GMT, \par \par \uc2  unchanged from opening levels. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around \par \par \uc2  42.3 to the euro to keep the crown from strengthening. In its \par \par \uc2  latest round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, the bank bid the \par \par \uc2  crown up to 42.315 to the euro after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currence\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed over \par \par \uc2  the 42.3 level. \par \par \uc2  "The crown is still at around the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels...but \par \par \uc2  no trading has been seen yet on the market," said Richard Brza \par \par \uc2  of CSOB bank. "We've seen no activity from both domestic and \par \par \uc2  foreign players." \par \par \uc2  "It's clear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been ready to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again...this is a factor preventing the crown from \par \par \uc2  firming, and on the other hand, there is not much reason for \par \par \uc2  easing at the moment," Brza added. \par \par \uc2  The crown was quoted at 42.85/90 to the dollar at 0910 GMT. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Javurek, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax \par \par \uc2  421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2h07ar9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
