\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to cap crown strength. \b0\par\par\uc2 179 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2000\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Feb 10 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the crown from firming, buying euros for crowns around 42.300-42.315 to the euro, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the same levels on Wednesday and has been doing so repeatedly since mid-December. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been active right above 42.300 (to the euro)," one dealer, who asked not to be identified, told Reuters. Another \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank added: "Yes, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in the market again." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively paid offers just above 42.300 to the euro on electronic broker systems. \par \par \uc2  The crown weakened slightly right after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 42.310/315 at 1037 GMT from about 42.285/300 just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Officials at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not immediately available to confirm dealer reports. ((Andrej Salner, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2a086yz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
