\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cenbank confirms crown  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2000\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Feb 1 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown at levels around 42.3 to the euro, confirming dealers' sightings of the bank earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  "We have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...We began somewhere below 42.3 and continued up to that level," said Frantisek Szulenyi, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets department. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the crown from strengthening over 42.3 to the euro repeatedly since mid-December, saying a firmer crown could hurt the economy. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it remained committed to defending the 42.3 level for the time being. \par \par \uc2  However, on Monday afternoon the crown traded at levels firmer than 42.3 without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepping in. \par \par \uc2  Local dealers said prior to Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appear on the market to weaken the crown. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , around 0900 GMT, the crown was quoted at 42.310/350 to the euro from 42.270/295 at the open. ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000