\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Stronger, awaiting Polish c/a data. \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2000\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 1 (Reuters) - The Czech and Slovak crowns gained on Tuesday, at one point prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, as investors bet long term capital inflows would continue to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Poland's zloty also opened firmer ahead of key current account data due at 1300 GMT that analysts will scour for signs of an export recovery. \par \par \uc2  But the rand hovered at 6.300 per dollar, near recent lows, despite credit growth numbers that showed South Africa's long-awaited economic recovery was not yet stoking inflation. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone's waiting for the Polish number. Until we get a good one, markets are going to remain cautious on Poland. It all hangs off exports," West LB economist Tim Ash said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect a December current account deficit of around $1.2 billion, after $1.15 billion in November, but a smaller number will be rewarded with strong zloty gains. \par \par \uc2  At 1015 GMT, the zloty rose to 2.75 percent above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rate from 2.48 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  FLAT POSTIONS AHEAD OF THE FED \par \par \uc2  Analysts and traders said most investors had flat positions going into the U.S. Federal Reserve's two day policy meeting, which starts today, with a 25 basis point hike widely expected. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which meets on Thursday, is also expected to raise rates by 25 bp. A mirror rates rise should help stem some of the recent volatility that has rattled emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegged to dollar/euro baskets. \par \par \uc2  Still, flat investor positions did not stop Slovakia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 42.3 crowns to the euro to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciating and choking off growth. At 1030 GMT, the unit stood at 42.32. \par \par \uc2  "The bank keeps on coming in at that level, but while people still see some long term upside there's more caution," Ash said. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown also reversed some of Monday's losses that were prompted by news the government would set up an offshore account to deposit privatisation revenues that might otherwise be repatriated and boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((John Paul Rathbone, London Capital Markets unit, tel 44 171 542 5110, fax 542 5285, john.rathbone@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw2103500\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
