\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says still ready to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2000\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Jan 27 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it remained ready to prevent the crown from firming over the 42.3 to the euro level at which it has repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-December. \par \par \uc2  "For the moment we do not see a reason for any change in the level at which we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the last time - 42.3 to the euro," Frantisek Szulenyi, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets department, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  When asked specifically whether the bank was prepared to prevent a firming over 42.3 to the euro, Szulenyi said: "For now yes." \par \par \uc2  He added that the bank had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent days since the crown was trading steadily above the 42.3 level. \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT, the crown was quoted at 42.320/345. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long said that it has a preferred range within which it wants to see the crown. It does not publish this range, however, but says it can move according to economic fundamentals, such as the trade situation. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak Statistical Office said on Tuesday that a surge in exports had slashed Slovakia's 1999 trade deficit to 45.7 billion crowns in 1999 after an 82.9 billion crown deficit the year before. \par \par \uc2  But the December deficit, at 7.6 billion crowns, was the second highest monthly deficit of the year. ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1r07isf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
