\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  crown calm, near earlier  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  level. \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2000\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Jan 26 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown was calm on Wednesday morning, but dealers said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to again approach 42.3 to the euro, the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a firming. \par \par \uc2  The crown was quoted at 42.335/375 to the euro at 0815 GMT, unmoved from opening levels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-December to keep the crown from strengthening beyond 42.3 to the euro. The bank has said, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level could change at any time depending on economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "Banks are long in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so we will probably approach 42.3 to the euro again in the near future," said Juraj Zabadal, a trader at Slovenska Sporitelna. "The question now is whether or not the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level has been moved after Tuesday's foreign trade figures." \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the Slovak Statistical Office said that Slovakia's trade deficit in 1999 reached 45.7 billion crowns compared with 82.9 billion crowns in the previous year. \par \par \uc2  The crown was quoted at 42.29/35 to the dollar at 0815 GMT. ((Andrej Salner, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba00000200