\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Slovak Dec inflation hits top end of target. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robin Shepherd \par \uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2000\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Slovakia's end year inflation rate came in at the top end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range on Wednesday, with consumer prices rising by 0.4 percent month-on-month in December and 14.2 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll of analysts conducted on Tuesday gave a mean average prediction of 0.33 percent for the month with annualised December inflation seen at 14.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Prior to the release of the data, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the crown firming through 42.3 to the euro but traders said the inflation figures were unlikely to move the market even at such a sensitive time. \par \par \uc2  "These data had no influence on market developments," said Branislav Matusek, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at ING Barings. \par \par \uc2  "Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has declared it is watching foreign trade data closely in determining the crown level it desires, the market's attention is likely to focus more on these figures ... The market will note other indicators, but they are unlikely to have an impact." \par \par \uc2  Jan Toth, chief economist at ING Barings in Bratislava, said the figures were a touch higher than expected and had been boosted by food and fuel prices. \par \par \uc2  These components of the inflation basket had probably been affected by seasonal and world pricing factors, however, rather than the amount of money circulating in the Slovak economy. \par \par \uc2  "So I would not expect monetary policy to tighten because of this," he told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has targeted core inflation at 4.5 to 5.8 percent for end-December 2000 but analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings of a credit crunch this year suggested that monetary policy may not be adjusted to achieving this aim at all costs. \par \par \uc2  "I believe there is a will in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to significantly reduce interest rates this year in order to avoid the situation which arose in the Czech Republic in the last two years," said Milos Bozek of J&T Securities. \par \par \uc2  "This would also be a tool for fighting an overvalued crown." \par \par \uc2  Bozek said many analysts partly attributed the recent deep recession in the Czech Republic to a failure of the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to begin cutting interest rates soon enough. \par \par \uc2  "Even if inflation is a bit above target they will not tighten because of the potential for a credit crunch," added Toth. ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1c03pya\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
