\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Steady in Europe, ignoring bond falls. \b0\par\par\uc2 883 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2000\par 13:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed to weaker in Europe on Wednesday, showing no clear reaction to interest rate fears that sent international bond yields to their highest levels since 1997. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Weakness in Polish Treasury bills, amid a rise in German Bund yields to more than two-year highs, had some impact on the zloty\tab   in early trade, said Jan Pudil, trader at West LB. But the unit later firmed to stand little changed despite reduced hopes that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be fully floated soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The zloty surged to near five-month highs ahead of a meeting between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry on a float, but fell on Tuesday after the government did not discuss the issue at its weekly meeting. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Finance Minister Jaroslaw Bauc said a period of stabilisation was needed before a decision would be made. \par \par \uc2  "Despite all this, we remain inclined to believe that the zloty will be floated during 1H2000 and that the PLN/EUR exchange rate will become the exchange rate on which markets will focus," said Deutsche Bank analyst Laura Papi in a daily note. \par \par \uc2  Papi and Pudil said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effectively free floating anyway as it can move in a 30 percent band. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty\tab      was bid around three percent stronger than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's parity level, firmer than Tuesday's 2.9 percent, and at 4.1890 against the euro versus 4.1950.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SOUTH AFRICA MULLS RATES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Africa's rand\tab   was little changed as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began a two-day meeting that may lower interest rates for the first time since November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economists are divided on whether the Reserve Bank will free the repo rate, which it fixed at 12 percent on November 25, now that the millennium rollover has passed without problem. Some think it will leave the rate on hold because of evidence of mounting growth and rising rates elsewhere in the world.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank said its Monetary Policy Committee would issue a statement on interest rates Thursday afternoon. The rand traded at 6.076 bid compared with 6.07 late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Israeli shekel\tab   was also steady despite losses in U.S. stocks and signs that Prime Minister Ehud Barak may have problems winning cabinet approval for his nominated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor David Klein.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its strongest levels since July on Tuesday, continuing to gain on expectations Klein would not cut interest rates drastically.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But local dealers said the market was now following the direction of U.S. equities, whose strength has sent Israeli shares soaring. U.S. stocks fell on Tuesday, with technology issues suffering particularly heavy losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reports that the cabinet was divided on Klein's appointment may also weigh on the shekel, which was bid around 4.1151 to the dollar compared with 4.1102 late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\tab   was little changed as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for a third day running, buying euros for crowns at around 42.3 to the euro. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      was recently bid near 42.235 to the euro.\par The Czech crown\tab \tab \tab continued to trade around the 36 to the euro level, weakening to 35.975 bid from 35.93 on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including the change versus late New York trade the previous day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the change in the year to date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , formerly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect new market norms. All other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are quoted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise or fall of the dollar or euro value.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first day of the current trading year, January 4.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   CLOSE\tab \tab IN 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab    35.98   35.95   0.08%   -0.28%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab  4.19    4.19    -0.06%  -0.05%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 254.7   254.58  0.05%   0.12%\par S