\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Central Europe firm, picture positive. \b0\par\par\uc2 789 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2000\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 11 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly firmer on Tuesday with the Polish zloty showing strength despite a delay in a decision to float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry. \par \par \uc2  Traders and analysts said that trading volumes had improved from last week, although they were not back up to pre-Christmas levels. \par \par \uc2  "We expect a decision on the zloty to be taken in the second quarter. Obviously strong privatisation inflows will drive the zloty stronger," said Stefan Kolek, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank. \par \par \uc2  By 1111 GMT, the zloty was trading at 4.174 bid to the euro little changed from the close of 4.1725. It was at 3.34 percent on the strong side of parity against its basket of dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  Poland's Finance Ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council on Monday concluded their meeting with no word on the flotation of the zloty when many had been expecting a decision or at least a timeframe for one. \par \par \uc2  The zloty currently trades in a 30 percent wide trading range and is devalued at 0.3 percent a month. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Central Europe, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at around 42.3 to the euro and the crown was trading at 42.219 bid in mid-morning trade. \par \par \uc2  "The fact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is marginal," said Kolek. "They cannot do anything in the long run." \par \par \uc2  Slovak bond yields dipped ahead of a 3.0 billion crown T-bond offering, ahead of strong anticipated demand. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown was little changed after Monday's release of December consumer price inflation, which came in higher than expected at 0.5 percent month on month. \par \par \uc2  The crown was at 35.972 bid to the euro, marginally weaker than 35.97 at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CNB) Vice-governor Zdenek Tuma said his bias on monetary policy remained neutral despite stronger-than-expected inflation in December, the daily Hospodarske Noviny said on Tuesday. In Hungary, the main news of the day was the addition of 200 million euros to a floating rate issue for a total of 600 million euros. \par \par \uc2  The forint was trading at compared 254.54 bid to the euro, little changed from 254.63 at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  In South Africa, the rand was firmer as the market braces for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings on Wednesday and Thursday this week, at which a further cut in interest rates is expected. \par \par \uc2  The rand was at 6.0710 bid to the dollar, little changed from late-Monday trade. \par \par \uc2  The Israeli shekel continued to rally against the dollar to its highest level in 4-1/2 months with the appointment of David Klein as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief. \par \par \uc2  It was trading at 4.1009 bid to the dollar. \par \par \uc2   ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, \par \par \uc2  including the change versus late New York trade the previous day \par \par \uc2  and the change in the year to date. \par \par \uc2   ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly \par \par \uc2  quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to \par \par \uc2  reflect new 