\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak crown slightly weaker, seen calm. \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRATISLAVA, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The Slovak crown\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par opened slightly weaker on Wednesday, with dealers saying they\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  did not expect any turbulence on the quiet market during the \par \par \uc2  day. \par \par \uc2      The crown was quoted at 42.350/450 to the euro at 0820 GMT, \par \par \uc2  unchanged from the open, but weaker from Tuesday's close at \par \par \uc2  42.300/400 to the euro. \par \par \uc2      "We opened a little bit down from Tuesday, and so far we \par \par \uc2  have seen only a couple of domestic banks buying \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \par \par \uc2  ING's Zuzana Rafajova. \par \par \uc2      "These buys have been made on low volumes and I don't see a \par \par \uc2  reason to expect anything special later on today," she added. \par \par \uc2      On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling \par \par \uc2  crowns for euros close to 42.3 to the euro. Monday's \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came at levels around 42.29 to the euro. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official monetary programme calls for \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against excess volatility but not against trends. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said they did not expect such developments on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      "I don't think the crown will streghten through 42.300 to \par \par \uc2  the euro today...It might happen only if somebody does it \par \par \uc2  deliberately," Rafajova said. \par \par \uc2      At 0825 GMT, the crown was quoted to the dollar with the \par \par \uc2  midpoint at 40.820. \par \par \uc2  ((Peter Javurek, Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax \par \par \uc2  421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw150826j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
