\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty calm after Polish telecom delay. \b0\par\par\uc2 830 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 1999\par 13:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 23 (Reuters) - Failure to agree a price for the sale of a stake in Polish telecommunications company TPSA did not make much a of a dent in the zloty as trading was slim ahead of the extended Christmas and millennium break. \par \par \uc2  "It had an effect, but so many people are happy to have their positions through to the New Year," said Nick Douch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  By 1140 GMT the zloty was trading at 4.165 bid to the euro, marginally higher than at the close of trade in New York, but slightly weaker than the 4.16 bid of morning trade on Wednesday. Against its basket of euros and dollars the zloty was 2.33 percent on the strong side of parity. \par \par \uc2  Poland on Wednesday rejected an offer by France Telecom  for a strategic stake in local phone group TPSA  and said it would call for fresh bids in the largest privatisation deal in the country's history. \par \par \uc2  Polish treasury minister Emil Wasacz said the French offer for a 25-35 percent stake in state-controlled TPSA had not met his expectations and that a fresh tender would be announced early in the New Year. \par \par \uc2  France Telecom, the sole bidder after U.S. SBC Communications  backed out in November due to a lack of clarity in market regulations, was believed to have offered $3.5 billion for a 30 percent stake, close to treasury demands. \par \par \uc2  The deal was said to have collapsed not so much because of the price, but due to the French firm's demands for full management control and 'get-out' clauses should a new telecoms law damage future profits. \par \par \uc2  Merrill Lynch said that while the bad news was evident in a six month delay there was a silver lining. \par \par \uc2  The cancellation clears the way for a new list of investors who came too late the first time or where circumstances have changed, Merrill said in a report. \par \par \uc2  "We believe Deutsche Telekom will undoubtedly be first on any advisors' wish list given their less than satisfactory position in PTC," Merrill said. The seasonal torpor in markets extended throughout emerging Europe, with the extent of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rise in the value of the crown becoming clear after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to $3.4 billion as of December 21 from $2.9 billion as of December 15. "The Slovaks have got to think what they will do. The problem with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they are practising it is that they are selling their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which adds to the money supply," said Douch. \par \par \uc2  The crown was little changed at 42.454 bid to the euro. \par \par \uc2  In South Africa, the prospect of bond markets closing until after the New Year limited appetite for rand trade. \par \par \uc2  The rand was at 6.1450 bid to the dollar. \par \par \uc2      ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange \par \par \uc2  rates, including the change versus late New York trade the \par \par \uc2  previous day and the change in the year to date. For the latest \par \par \uc2  live prices click on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  RICs. \par \par \uc2      ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the \par \par \uc2  euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are \par \par \uc2  quoted against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted \par \par \uc2  in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes \par \par \uc2  the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. \par \par \uc2      ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the \par \par \uc2  first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.16   36.17   -0.04%  3.89%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab   4.17    4.17    -0.07%  2.45%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab  254.29  254.32  -0.01%  1.23%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 42.40   42.32   0.18%   -1.40%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab  17,950  17,945  0.03%   63.93%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab  5.23    5.30    -1.32%  33.08%\par South Africa\tab \tab   6.14    6.14    0.01%   5.08%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    72.90   72.70   0.28%   18.34%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.169   4.169   -0.01%  1.21%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab   535,350 535,030 0.06%   69.54%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab   9.32    9.32    -0.03%  -5.32%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab   1.8200  1.8200  0.00%   50.77%\par Venezuela\tab \tab      644.00  644.00  0.00%   14.08%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab    536.30  536.30  0.00%   14.06%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore\tab \tab      1.670   1.665   0.30%   0.85%\par Hong Kong\tab \tab      7.769   7.770   -0.02%  0.29%\par China\tab \tab \tab    8.280   8.280   0.00%   0.00%\par Indonesia\tab \tab      7,045   7,080   -0.49%  -11.38%\par Thailand\tab \tab \tab 37.42   37.60   -0.48%  3.66%\par Philippines\tab \tab    40.15   40.30   -0.37%  4.69%\par Taiwan\tab \tab \tab   31.59   31.53   0.17%   -1.60%\par South Korea\tab \tab    1,130   1,131   -0.09%  -4.64%\par Ind