\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Slovak crown unmoved by bank sale. \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 1999\par 13:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 20 (Reuters) - The sale of the Slovak government's 24 percent stake in Czech bank CSOB for 400 million euros had been widely anticipated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and did not renew upward pressure on the Slovak crown. \par \par \uc2  However, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said that the prospect of larger privatisations and a deepening of Slovak debt markets would add to upward pressures on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming year. \par \par \uc2  "Volumes in the market are slim. The sale of CSOB had been expected," said Stefan Kolek, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak crown was trading 42.323 bid to the euro by 1102 GMT, slightly weaker from the New York close Friday of 42.27 to the euro and little changed from early morning levels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in an attempt to halt the rise in the value of the crown, to the extent that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $39 million last week, reflecting purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Strategists say that given limited foreign participation in the Slovak crown markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's task has been relatively easy so far, but that could change in 2000. \par \par \uc2  Privatisations such as that for bank Slovenska Sporitelna should also keep the crown strong. \par \par \uc2  "There will be more Slovak Eurobond issues, liquidity will be improved and the finance ministry wants to start a tapping system similar to the Hungarians," said Kolek. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, markets were quiet in the run-up to Christmas. \par \par \uc2  There was little movement in the Czech crown ahead of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting, with most analysts saying that a rate cut is unlikely. \par \par \uc2  The crown was trading at 35.981 bid to the euro, slightly weaker than 3.59 at the New York close. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian forint was steady at 253.79 bid to the euro, compared with 253.97 on Friday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key two week rate by 25 basis points to 14.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  The only Hungarian data due for release this week is October retail sales. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty was stronger at 4.1940 bid to the euro, up from 4.21 bid at the New York close after more details emerged of the country's proposed sterilisation account for privatisation inflows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz said on Monday that 40 percent of next year's privatisation inflows should be kept on a special hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to facilitate sovereign debt financing. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvck07wb9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
