\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weaker in Europe on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 705 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1999\par 12:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LONDON, Dec 16 (Reuters) - Talk of crown sales by the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  enlivened quiet emerging European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade on Thursday, weakening the crown\tab   from 10-week highs against the euro despite a denial from the bank that it was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par Local dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold crowns\tab      at around 35.80 to the euro, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was not active in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened to 36.005 to the euro after the initial report from 35.725 in early trade and 35.80 late on Wednesday. Even after the denial the crown remained weaker on the day, at 35.855.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Analysts have been expecting for weeks that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it would be worried a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hurt the fragile economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "Thirty-five point eight is getting to quite strong levels. When they started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  last time (in October) it was at these levels and then it went all the way up to 37," said Jan Pudil, trader at West LB. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said soon after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports that it would not discuss monetary policy at a regular board meeting underway. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also a focus for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\tab  , which was softer after two days of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action to stop its appreciation.\par The crown\tab      was quoted at 42.36 to the euro compared with 42.28 late on Wednesday and 1999 highs of 42.087 reached before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began making weaker bids for its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Marian Jusko said on Thursday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meant the crown would not firm over 42.3 to the euro, Czech news agency CTK reported.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty\tab   strengthened to 0.85 percent above the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's parity level from 0.67 percent on Wednesday ahead of the release later in the day of key industrial output data for November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HypoVereinsbank said it expected output to have increased 13 percent from the previous year, which should keep the zloty above parity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty\tab      was trading at 4.234 to the euro, against 4.2260 on Wednesday, when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left interest rates unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including the change versus late New York trade the previous day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the change in the year to date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , formerly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect new market norms. All other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are quoted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise or fall of the dollar or euro value.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first day of the current trading year, January 4.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab    LATEST  PREV   PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab  CLOSE\tab      in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab    35.86   35.75   0.32%   3.05%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab  4.23    4.21    0.56%   4.03%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 254.59  253.91  0.27%   1.35%\par Slovakia\tab \tab      42.37   42.28   0.21%   -1.47%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 17,915  17,940  -0.14%  63.61%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab 5.60    5.54    1.08%   42.49%\par South Africa\tab \tab  6.14    6.15    -0.18%  5.06%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab   73.85   73.50   0.48%   19.89%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab  4.186   4.186   0.01%   1.63%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab  528,400 530,150 -0.33%  67.34%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab  9.34    9.34    0.05%   -5.08%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab  1.8490  1.8470  0.11%   53.18%\par Venezuela\tab \tab     642.90  642.90  0.00%   13.89%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab   536.60  536.60  0.00%   14.12%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2