\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Czech crown gains, Slovaks  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 927 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1999\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LONDON, Dec 15 (Reuters) - The Czech crown\tab   strengthened to fresh 10-week highs against the euro on Wednesday following news of an acceleration of economic growth, while reports of a second day of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\tab   below its 1999 highs.\par Other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region were little changed, with Poland's zloty\tab   and Israel's shekel\tab   steady before the release of inflation data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although Czech third-quarter gross domestic product data was widely leaked on Tuesday, confirmation that the fragile economy was making a mild recovery gave the crown a slight boost that took it to its firmest rate against the euro since early October.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  GDP grew by 0.8 percent year-on-year in the third quarter, compared with forecasts for 0.5-0.7 percent and growth of 0.4 percent in the second quarter. But retail sales data released at the same time was less encouraging, showing an annual fall of 1.6 percent in October. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The crown\tab      was bid around 35.829 to the euro, off its strongest levels of the day at 35.790 but still stronger than 35.86 late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts expected worries that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the crown to cap its appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SLOVAK INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOTED\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Across the border in Slovakia, dealers reported the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for a second day to keep the crown\tab      at the weaker levels it orchestrated on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said the bank was bidding for the crown at 42.3 to the euro, similar to the rates it bid on Tuesday in its first ever \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market's so thin at the moment they (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) can probably do what they want and get away with it," said Nick Douch, emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Barclays Capital.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The crown was trading at 42.288 after the reported \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , compared with 42.32 late on Tuesday and 1999 highs of 42.087 early that day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The focus in the zloty\tab      market was the release later in the day of inflation figures for November, expected to show a one percent monthly rise in consumer prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ahead of the figures the zloty was little changed at 0.51 percent stronger than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's parity level versus Tuesday's close of 0.59 percent. It was bid at 4.230 to the euro against 4.237.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The shekel was little changed near four-month highs following strong gains on Monday and Tuesday, which were triggered by historic peace talks with Syria and improved international sentiment on Israel's credit rating and stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inflation data to be published later in the day was expected to show consumer prices rose by as much as 0.2 percent in November. The shekel was trading at 4.1846 to the dollar versus 4.1856 late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hungary's forint\tab \tab \tab was little changed at 2.24 percent above parity, at the strong end of its trading band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par News on Tuesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will reduce its monthly devaluation rate in the first half of next year, with another cut possible in the second half, meant the exchange rate mechanism would remain broadly unchanged in 2000, Deutsche Bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Romania's leu\tab   strengthened against the dollar as the market remained undisturbed by the ousting of Prime Minister Radu Vasile on Monday. The leu was quoted at 17,860 to the dollar against around 17,900 at Tuesday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including the change versus late New York trade the previous day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the change in the year to date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , formerly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect new market norms. All other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are quoted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise or fall of the dollar or euro value.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first day of the current trading year, January 4.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab    LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab  CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab    35.83   35.85   -0.06%  2.96%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab  4.23    4.22    0.22%   4.00%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 253.49  253.70  -0.08%  0.92%\par Slovakia\tab \tab      42.26   42.32   -0.14%  -1.72%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 17,860  17,940  -0.45%  63.11%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab 5.40    5.40    0.00%   37.40%\par South Africa\tab \tab  6.12    6.13    -0.11%  4.76%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab   74.55   74.65   -0.13%  21.02%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab  4.185   4.183   0.05%   1.60%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab  529,700 529,160 0.10%   67.75%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab  9.39    9.40    -0.06%  -4.55%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab  1.8520  1.8520  0.00%   53.43%\par Venezuela\tab \tab     642.90  642.90  0.00%   13.89%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab   537.30  537.30  0.00%   14.27%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore\tab \tab     1.678   1.680   -0.12%  1.32%\par Hong Kong\tab \tab     7.775   7.774   0.00%   0.37%\par China\tab \tab \tab   8.279   8.279   0.00%   0.00%\par Indonesia\tab \tab     7,080   7,180   -1.39%  -10.94%\par Thailand\tab \tab      38.42   38.56   -0.36%  6.43%\par Philippines\tab \tab   40.65   40.58   0.17%   6.00%\par Taiwan\tab \tab \tab  31.61   31.55   0.17%   -1.54%\par South Korea\tab \tab   1,134   1,133   0.09%   -4.30%\par India\tab \tab \tab   43.51   43.45   0.14%   2.41%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcf085d8\par }\page {\par\fs20{