\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  deputy PM praises cbank crown  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1999\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Dec 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Prime Minister for the Economy Ivan Miklos said Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown was good news for current account deficit prospects. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the exchange rate prior (to Tuesday) was optimal from the point of view of maintaining competitiveness and thus also for the current account and trade deficit. I thus agree with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told journalists. \par \par \uc2  Miklos said that a rate of around 43 to the euro was "balanced from the perspective of positives and negatives". \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid down the crown to 42.15 to the euro and in mid-afternoon to 42.3 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade hit its strongest level since the creation of the euro, at 42.087 according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  "The National Bank really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because in its monetary programme it has as one of its aims a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not large fluctuations," Ivan Paska, a spokesman for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "One of the reasons for the strengthening was entry into the EU integration process... The most pragmatic reason, however, is that the end of the year is drawing near and banks are closing their positions," he added. \par \par \uc2  ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par 