\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in line with policy. \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1999\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Dec 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Ivan Pasko said on Tuesday that the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown following a firming caused by last Friday's invitation to begin accession talks with the European Union. \par \par \uc2  "The National Bank really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because in its monetary programme it has as one of its aims a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not large fluctuations," Pasko told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "One of the reasons for the strengthening was entry into the EU integration process... The most pragmatic reason, however, is that the end of the year is drawing near and banks are closing their positions," he added. \par \par \uc2  The bank bid down the crown to 42.15 to the euro and then 42.20 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade hit its strongest level since the creation of the euro, at 42.087 according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  "It seems that the crown began to firm in the last few days more than we considered to be healthy," Pasko said. \par \par \uc2  Pasko would not comment on how heavy the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been, but several dealers told Reuters they thought it unlikely that more than five million euros had been used. \par \par \uc2  ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvce084wu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100