\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS -  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  weakens crown. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrej Salner \par \uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1999\par 17:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Dec 14 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown for the first time on Tuesday, dampening enthusiasm for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Friday's invitation from the European Union for Bratislava to begin accession talks. \par \par \uc2  The bank bid down the crown to 42.15 to the euro and in mid afternoon to 42.3 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade hit its strongest level since the creation of the euro, at 42.087 according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  "The National Bank really \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because in its monetary programme it has as one of its aims a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not large fluctuations," Ivan Paska, a spokesman for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "One of the reasons for the strengthening was entry into the EU integration process...The most pragmatic reason however is that the end of the year is drawing near and banks are closing their positions," he added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move was endorsed by Deputy Prime Minister for the Economy Ivan Miklos. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the exchange rate prior (to Tuesday) was optimal from the point of view of maintaining competitiveness and thus also for the current account and trade deficit. I thus agree with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told journalists. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  DECLINES DETAILS \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the volume of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but one dealer who asked not to be named said he thought that around 30 million euros had been used. "I think that they've done around 30 million euros today...But it seems that they've accomplished what they wanted to accomplish," he said. \par \par \uc2  Branislav Matusek, a trader at ING Barings, said: "It seems like they are not trying to change the trend, but only to maintain liquidity in the market." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the strengthening pressure on the crown came mainly from non-resident banks amid low liquidity, due to rising expectations of investment inflows after the EU issued its invitation. \par \par \uc2  The European Union on Friday invited Slovakia at its Helsinki Summit to begin talks on accession to the bloc. \par \par \uc2  "Non-residents have been selling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few days driving the crown up...Their main reasons probably are the expectations of improved ratings next year, EU accession talks and recent improvements in the balance of payments," said Dusan Svitek of Slovenska Sporitelna. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Brigita Schmognerova said on Monday she would prefer the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap crown strength before the end of the year, as it could complicate the task of calculating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk for local companies. \par \par \uc2  However, the finance ministry said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was a matter for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it was confident the bank would take steps to ensure exchange rate stability for the crown. \par \par \uc2  Late in November, when the crown was trading close to 43 to the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said it was satisfied with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level. Miklos said then that a further strengthening would be negative for the economy. \par \par \uc2  ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax 421-7-5341-8403, bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvce084fk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
