\par\par \b \uc2  Slovak FinMin says cbank to ensure crown stability. \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 1999\par 14:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Dec 14 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Ministry said after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday it was confident that the bank would ensure the stability of the Slovak crown. \par \par \uc2  "Exchange rate policy is fully in the hands of the National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) and we have no doubt that the NBS will undertake adequate steps to promote a stable exchange rate," Finance Ministry spokesman Peter Svec told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the crown for the first time ever on Tuesday morning after Friday's invitation from the European Union to begin accession talks boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The bank bid down the crown to 42.15 to the euro and then 42.20 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade hit its strongest level since the creation of the euro, at 42.087 according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  flew in the face of comments by Finance Minister Brigita Schmognerova on Monday. The minister said she would prefer the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap crown strength before the end of the year, as it could complicate the task of calculating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk for local companies. She did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  The bank said its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with one of its monetary policy aims of curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  At 1151 GMT the crown was quoted at 42.147/227 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvce084em\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
