\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Zloty dips, Czech, Slovak stay strong. \b0\par\par\uc2 785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 1999\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LONDON, Dec 13 (Reuters) - Poland's zloty\tab   weakened in thin emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief cooled hopes for a quick move to fully float the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Hanna Gronkiewicz-Waltz said on Friday she was taken by surprise by Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz's statement that a decision on floating the zloty would be made soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The zloty\tab     , which surged almost three percentage points against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's parity rate last week after Balcerowicz's statement, dipped to 1.53 percent above parity from 2.07 percent on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Gronkiewicz-Waltz said she thought the zloty would start to be freely traded at some point in 2000 though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and government, which must both approve the decision, were not discussing the issue.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts say a full float would not move the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  much because it is well within the boundaries of its trading band of 15 percentage points either side of parity. But it could provide a small psychological boost.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's positive because it sends a good signal of confidence to the market," said Banque Paribas analyst Sonia Hellemann, who expects a float around February or March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CROWN SEEN FIRMING\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Czech crown\tab \tab      , buoyed by demand from foreign business investors, was little changed near its strongest levels against the euro since October 4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bid at 35.87 to the euro versus 35.84 on Friday, showed no reaction to producer prices data that met expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prices in November rose 0.2 percent from the previous month and 2.4 percent on the year, compared with analysts' forecasts for 0.3 percent and 2.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hellemann said the crown could firm to 35.6 and then 35.2 if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to hold back from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Slovak\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crown\tab \tab \tab traded around record highs against the euro amid expectations the European Union's decision on Friday to start membership talks with Slovakia will boost foreign investment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The crown was bid around 42.21 to the euro from Friday's close of 42.25.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Israel's shekel\tab   was bid firmer at 4.214 to the dollar from 4.219. The International Monetary Fund on Sunday said Israel required a more balanced mix of monetary and fiscal policies to sustain its nascent economic recovery\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par An IMF mission visiting Israel said in a report it strongly supports the government's decision to target a budget deficit of 2.5 percent of gross domestic product in 2000 and urged the government to resist pressures to widen the deficit or finance higher spending through a tax increase.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including the change versus late New York trade the previous day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the change in the year to date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , formerly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflect new market norms. All other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are quoted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise or fall of the dollar or euro value.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first day of the current trading year, January 4.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab   LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab    35.87   35.85   0.07%   3.07%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab  4.21    4.19    0.41%   3.38%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 254.11  254.07  0.02%   1.16%\par Slovakia\tab \tab      42.21   42.35   -0.34%  -1.84%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 17,897  17,880  0.10%   63.44%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab 5.40    5.40    0.00%   37.40%\par South Africa\tab \tab  6.11    6.12    -0.09%  4.52%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab   74.50   74.55   -0.07%  20.94%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab  4.214   4.219   -0.11%  2.31%\par Turkey\tab \tab \tab  525,980 525,700 0.05%   66.58%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \p