\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -No sign of CNB but crown nervous. \b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 13:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The Czech crown came back from its highs on Friday in thin nervous trading with traders wary of the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had not so far materialised. \par \par \uc2  By 1139 GMT the crown was at 36.095 bid to the euro, down from a day high of 35.95 and 36.02 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The Czech National Bank has not been in as far as I know," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  "Trading is shallow and a bit nervous," he added. \par \par \uc2  The crown had gone as high as 35.950 to the euro in the wake of Thursday's 25 basis point cut in interest rates to 5.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say, however, that the rate cut will do little to hinder the crown's advance. \par \par \uc2  "After deciding on November 25 to cut rates by 25 basis points (without succeeding to move the exchange rate in response to the cut), and after it unsuccessfully attempted to talk the koruna weaker, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now left to consider another round of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the relentless appreciation pressure on the koruna," CSFB said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  CSFB believes that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the crown breaks through 36 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CNB) Governor Josef Tosovsky said on Thursday the rate cut to 5.25 percent was aimed at meeting the bank's end-2000 inflation target. \par \par \uc2  Tosovsky said the rate cut was not expected to have a direct impact on the crown, which the CNB was still closely watching in case it needed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak\b0 \highlight\uc2  crown held on to some of the gains it made on the coattails of the Czech unit. \par \par \uc2  It was trading at 43.071 bid to the euro, still close to its day high of 43.039. The Polish zloty was in thrall to political developments, awaiting President Alexander Kwasniewski's decision on whether to sign a key tax bill. \par \par \uc2  The decision, on which the future of market darling Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz hangs, will be made Sunday at the latest. \par \par \uc2  The zloty was at 4.2857 bid to the euro, stronger than 4.30 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  "I think it will be signed, this is just political posturing," said the trader. \par \par \uc2  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab    LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab  CLOSE\tab      in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.14   35.9