\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  cbank says still prepared to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1999\par 16:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, May 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovak central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Vladimir Masar said on Thursday that the bank remained ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets against fluctuations which were not based on fundamentals. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times during the week in the face of sustained downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Masar said the weakening that this had led to was not based on economic fundamentals. "In the development of basic economic indicators, no significant deviations took place recently...the NBS (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against fluctuations as it did today," Masar told journalists. \par \par \uc2  He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as of May 18 were $2.7368 billion. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a united front in defence of the crown on Thursday morning, helping the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mount a moderate recovery after weeks of steady decline. \par \par \uc2  It was quoted at 46.599/799 to the euro at 1410 GMT from records lows of about 42 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Masar said the government's plans to bring order to the public finances and impose an import surcharge were a good sign. But they must be implemented. \par \par \uc2  "I see as very positive the clear signal sent by the government of the Slovak Republic...Government as well as politicians in the coalition clearly declared their will to solve problems." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to support the crown on Thursday and said exchange rate developments had priority over interest rates. The government pledged to increase VAT to raise money for the state budget and also to impose an import surcharge. \par \par \uc2  The government aims cut the fiscal deficit to around two percent of GDP this year and to halve the current account deficit from over 10 percent of gross domestic product last year. Deputy Premier for the Economy Ivan Miklos conceded that the fiscal target would be difficult to meet but that Wednesday's measures were a big step in the right direction. ((Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-5341-8402, fax, 421-7-5341-8403 bratislava.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5k00d0w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
