\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovak \highlight\uc2  Natl Bker -3: Mkts Stable After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1999\par 17:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "The koruna exchange rate is now stable, it seems that the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been effective," Masar commented. \par \par \uc2  "If the government loses its determination for economic reform, the exchange rate would again reflect it," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice Governor Marian Jusko said, although he added that the bank isn't planning to review its monetary plan for 1999. \par \par \uc2  Jusko said the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were aimed at stopping the continued depreciation of the koruna. He and other bank officials declined to say exactly how much the bank spent defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but said the $60 million figure published by the media was fairly accurate. \par \par \uc2  Bank officials added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves hadn't been jeopardized by the series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, and quoted reserves at $2.74 billion on May 18, down only slightly from $2.75 billion May 12. \par \par \uc2  Masar admitted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have had a negative effect on interest rates, deposits and development of finances in the country but said it wasn't possible to avoid the problems. \par \par \uc2  He added that he realizes the economic reforms announced by the government will be tough on citizens. \par \par \uc2  "I do realize that the government has to adapt a handful of unpopular measures that are politically sensitive," he said. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the government responded to the growing crisis Thursday morning by pledging to rebalance some value added taxes, liberalize regulated prices, and cut some state administration and welfare spending. \par \par \uc2  There are also proposals for a short-term import tariff on some goods. \par \par \uc2  Slovak Premier Mikulas Dzurinda said specific dates and figures in the plan won't be announced until after further debate. \par \par \uc2  The koruna rebounded Thursday after the government's plans were announced and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of trading Thursday, the euro was quoted at SKK46.870-SKK46.920, well above Wednesday lows of SKK48.400-SKK48.600. The dollar was quoted at SKK43.953-44.064, down from SKK45.550-SKK45.650 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Andrea Lorinczova; 4217-544-35829 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-05-99 \par \par \uc2  1544GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5k03v60\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
